    <sys:String x:Key="Str.Info.HowTo">How to use it</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str.Info.HowToText">Add a folder with photos using the + button in the Library section; the app indexes it, including subfolders, without modifying or copying any file.|Select a folder in the tree to see only its photos (including subfolders); click the “Library” title to show all photos again.|Double-click a photo (or press Enter) to open it full screen; zoom with the mouse wheel, pan by dragging.|Right-click a source folder: Rescan (new / deleted photos) or Remove from library.|Source folders and the theme can also be managed from Options (gear icon).|Select one or more photos (Ctrl / Shift + click, Ctrl+A), then right-click → Add to album / Add tag. Click the “Albums” title to see albums as a grid of cards; double-click opens an album.|The selected photo's tags appear in the right panel: “+” adds, “×” removes. Click a tag on the left to see all photos that have it.|The search field (Ctrl+F) filters the displayed photos by file name, tags and albums; the name sort order is changed from the list next to it. R rotates the selected photo by 90° (the original file is not modified).|Batch rename (first icon in the top bar): choose a folder on disk, type a pattern (e.g. Greece_{counter:000}) and see the new names before applying. Photos already in the library keep their albums, tags and rotation.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str.Info.Shortcuts">Keyboard shortcuts</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="Str.Info.ShortcutsText">Enter=Open the selected photo full screen|Esc=Close full-screen view / logo view / this dialog|← / →=Previous / next photo (full screen)|Home / End=First / last photo (full screen)|+ / −=Zoom in / out (full screen)|0=Fit to screen|1=Actual size (1:1)|Ctrl+A=Select all photos in the grid|Ctrl / Shift + click=Multiple selection in the grid|R=Rotate the photo 90° (grid or full screen)|Ctrl+F=Focus the search field|Esc (in search)=Clear the search</sys:String>
